Candidates checked and rejected:
- Template injection through [branch.*] keys in _rs_direct_commit (repo-sync ~L740): a key with a tab or newline could fake a row, but the values file is the consumer's own .config/bootstrap.toml; no trust boundary is crossed. The key only reaches _rs_log; _rs_branch_exists gets only main or develop, quoted.
- Command injection: the rendered value reaches the shell only quoted, in [[ ]] comparisons and git show-ref. Nothing is evaluated.
- Bypass of branch protection through hook filtering in _rs_context: removes only --branch pairs of main or develop, only for direct_commit = true or a missing branch; consumer pre-commit.yaml is consumer-owned. Intended feature.
- A missing branch drops its pair: a develop created after a sync has no hook until the next setup:configs. Hardening gap, not exploitable.
- SKIP=...no-commit-to-branch in precommit_safety_net (merge L78-81): the run makes no commit; caller SKIP kept; env vars trusted.
- The direct_commit boolean check: non-bool stops the sync with code 2; keys outside main/develop rejected.
